Generic single-database configuration.

📌 Database Setup & Migration Guide (PostgreSQL + SQLAlchemy + Alembic)

This project uses PostgreSQL as the database and Alembic for schema migrations.
Follow the steps below to set up the database and run migrations.

🔧 1. Install PostgreSQL

Download PostgreSQL from the official page:

https://www.postgresql.org/download/


During installation you will choose:

PostgreSQL password for user postgres

Default port: 5432

After installation, open pgAdmin or use terminal to create a database.

🗄️ 2. Create a Database
Using pgAdmin

Open pgAdmin

Right-click Databases → Create → Database

Name it (example): multiagent_db

OR CLI
createdb multiagent_db

🔐 3. Set Environment Variables

Create a .env file in the backend folder:

DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/multiagent_db
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key_here
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60

📦 4. Install Dependencies

Make sure your virtual environment is activated:

pip install alembic sqlalchemy asyncpg python-dotenv

🔧 5. Initialize Alembic (Run Once)
alembic init alembic


This creates an alembic folder and alembic.ini.

📝 6. Edit alembic.ini

Find the line:

sqlalchemy.url = driver://user:pass@localhost/dbname


Replace with:

sqlalchemy.url = %(DATABASE_URL)s

🔧 7. Edit alembic/env.py

Inside env.py, import your models:

from app.models.user import User
from app.db import Base
target_metadata = Base.metadata

🏗️ 8. Create & Run Migrations
Whenever models change, generate a migration:
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "added provider fields"

Apply migration:
alembic upgrade head

⬅️ Roll Back Migration

Undo the last migration:

alembic downgrade -1

🔍 Verify the Database

You can check tables in pgAdmin or by using:

SELECT * FROM users;
